mission "The Battle of Lantern Passage"
    name "The Battle of Lantern Passage"
    description "Defeat the syndicate's hired escort squadron before it can seize the scholar's charts."
    source "Saint Brigid"
    destination "Port de Lune"
    reward 1980
    speaker offer "Commodore Wycliffe"
    speaker visit "Commodore Wycliffe"
    speaker complete "Commodore Wycliffe"
    to offer
        has "The Company Beneath the Sand: done"
    objective kills 2
    battlefield "Lantern Passage" 9000 3200
    enemy "Wycliffe's Vanguard"
    enemy "Wycliffe's Second"
    on offer
        conversation
            `Defeat the syndicate's hired escort squadron before it can seize the scholar's charts.`
            `Commodore Wycliffe studies you for a moment. "The old sea charter settled one war, but it did not settle the past. The lost expedition sailed west under a sealed order, and its wake is stirring every ambitious captain in these waters."
            choice
                `(I will help uncover what happened.)`
                    accept
                `(Tell me what you are not saying.)`
                    goto details
                `(I have no wish to be drawn into another quarrel.)`
                    close
            label details
                `Commodore Wycliffe lowers their voice. "The maps were altered, the convoy erased from the books, and someone has been buying witnesses. Follow the evidence, not the flags."`
                choice
                    `(Then I will take the matter in hand.)`
                        accept
                    `(Not today.)`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The Battle of Lantern Passage. Defeat the syndicate's hired escort squadron before it can seize the scholar's charts."
    on visit
        conversation
            `Commodore Wycliffe receives you at Port de Lune. The evidence fits another piece into the puzzle: the expedition was not searching for gold alone, but for a place deliberately removed from every official chart.`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Commodore Wycliffe thanks you. "Every answer makes the sea less simple, captain. Yet the truth belongs to the people who live here, not to the first crown or company that can put a seal upon it."`
        log "Completed The Battle of Lantern Passage. Received 1980 gold. Defeat the syndicate's hired escort squadron before it can seize the scholar's charts."
